# Read-only DLPack views of a simulation (D[python-dlpack]), scenario
# sanitize of Driver/Inputs/python_dlpack.py, under compute-sanitizer:
# views of two parts handed to a stream of a consumer, read by the CUDA
# driver, and a tensor read after its simulation has ended, with no access
# beyond a buffer and no read of memory that nothing has written.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda, compute-sanitizer, python-api
#
# RUN: %compute_sanitizer --tool memcheck --error-exitcode 1 %mdir_python \
# RUN:   %S/../Driver/Inputs/python_dlpack.py %S/../Driver/Inputs/dipeptide GPU sanitize 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %compute_sanitizer --tool initcheck --error-exitcode 1 %mdir_python \
# RUN:   %S/../Driver/Inputs/python_dlpack.py %S/../Driver/Inputs/dipeptide GPU sanitize 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s

# CHECK: views of two parts, a tensor that outlives its simulation
# CHECK: dlpack sanitize passed
# CHECK: ERROR SUMMARY: 0 errors
